 "sentences": [
  "Employees can log in, view their point balance, browse available rewards, and redeem them instantly.",
  "We want to make the process as seamless and engaging as possible.",
  "Yes, we generally favor the Flask framework for building web APIs.",
  "We'll also be using Git for version control, so ensure that you're familiar with our branching strategy and pull request process.",
  "I'll provide you with some initial tasks to get you started, and we can schedule regular check-ins to discuss your progress and any questions you may have.",
  "Remember, I'm here to support you, so don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "You never know who you'll meet, and having a physical reminder of your connection can be valuable.",
  "Lastly, don\u2019t be afraid to join in on discussions and ask questions.",
  "It's important that we maintain consistency across our codebases.",
  "So, from now on, I need you to ensure that you always end function argument names with '_x'.",
  "This will help us maintain a clear and consistent style.",
  "Also, when naming classes, use all uppercase letters.",
  "This is a standard we're implementing to improve readability and maintain consistency with our Python code.",
  "Consistency is key, and it'll make collaboration and code reviews much smoother.",
  "If you have any questions or need clarification on anything we've discussed, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "I want to emphasize the importance of consistency in our code.",
  "From now on, I'd like you to end function argument names with '_f' and always end method names with '_md'."
 ],
